Package: poisselect
Type: Package
Title: Poisson Selection Model for Count Data
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person("Finn", "Metzler", role = c("aut", "cre"),
    email = "finn.metzler@stud.uni-bamberg.de")
Description: Maximum likelihood estimation of a Poisson selection model for
    count data that are only observed for a selected subsample. The outcome
    equation is a Poisson regression with a log-normal heterogeneity term,
    the selection equation is a probit, and the two error terms are jointly
    normal. The likelihood integral is approximated by Gauss-Hermite
    quadrature and evaluated on the log scale with the log-sum-exp trick.
    Includes print, summary, plot, predict, coef, vcov and logLik methods
    and a data simulator for the model.
